window.docContents[5].resolve({"/Design-restrictions/Syntax/#Core-C______--Design-restrictions--Syntax":{"contents":"In C++17 the branch of an if and the body of a loop may be a single statement without braces. An else then belongs to the nearest if without an else (N4659 §9.4.1 ¶1).Core C++ requires braces around every branch and every body, so if (x == 0) x = 1; is a syntax error, .With mandatory braces the grammar of Core C++ is LL(1), a theorem checked in Lean, . The parser is recursive descent, with one function per nonterminal. A brace closes every branch, so no else needs a disambiguation rule.\n\n","context":"Core C++\u0009Design restrictions","header":"9.3. Syntax","id":"/Design-restrictions/Syntax/#Core-C______--Design-restrictions--Syntax"}});